# Deny everything, then name what the wheel build actually reads. An allow-list
# rather than a deny-list because the interesting failure is the silent one: a new
# directory at the root (a fixture set, a vendored upstream checkout) landing in the
# build context and invalidating every cached layer without anyone noticing.
*

!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!pyproject.toml
!crates
!python

# maturin reads `readme` and the licence out of pyproject.toml's metadata, and fails
# the build if the files they name are absent.
!README.md
!LICENSE
!NOTICE

# Re-excluded from the directories admitted above.
crates/**/target
python/**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.so
